[91m│ # Communication model of fuzzilli with V8                                    │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ ## Source code                                                               │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ On a low level, Fuzzilli communicates with v8 through the REPRL protocol,    │[0m
[91m│ implemented on the fuzzer side by the libreprl C library in                  │[0m
[91m│ `Sources/libreprl/`. The main way of using the library is through the        │[0m
[91m│ following three functions:                                                   │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ `reprl_create_context()` this creates a new, empty REPRL context to be used  │[0m
[91m│ by the following APIs.                                                       │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ `reprl_initialize_context(ctx, argv, envp)` this initializes the given       │[0m
[91m│ context and sets the argv and envp vectors to use for the child processes.   │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ `reprl_execute(ctx, code)` this executes the given code and returns the exit │[0m
[91m│ status. If necessary, a new child process is created for this. This involves │[0m
[91m│ creating pipes, forking itself, then setting filedescriptors, and using      │[0m
[91m│ `execve` to execute the d8 binary. A child process can be reused for         │[0m
[91m│ multiple executions, thus increasing fuzzing performance as the overhead of  │[0m
[91m│ fork and execve are removed.                                                 │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ ## Coverage                                                                  │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ Coverage information are being monitored through shared memory. On the side  │[0m
[91m│ of v8 it is monitored through SanitizerCoverage module of Clang compiler (   │[0m
[91m│ https://clang.llvm.org/docs/SanitizerCoverage.html ) Through shared memory   │[0m
[91m│ information about edges are shared with fuzzilli which implements counter    │[0m
[91m│ for error and covered branches of the V8 code in                             │[0m
[91m│ Sources/libcoverage/coverage.c                                               │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
