[91m│ File: /Users/tarun/v8/v8/test/fuzzer/README.md                               │[0m
[91m│ Size: 3513 bytes                                                             │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ Content:                                                                     │[0m
[91m│ # How to make a libFuzzer fuzzer in V8                                       │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ This document describes how to make a new libFuzzer fuzzer for V8. A general │[0m
[91m│ introduction to libFuzzer can be found                                       │[0m
[91m│ [here](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/master/testing/libfu │[0m
[91m│ zzer/README.md).                                                             │[0m
[91m│ In short, libFuzzer is an in-process coverage-driven evolutionary fuzzer.    │[0m
[91m│ libFuzzer serves you with a sequence of byte arrays that you can use to test │[0m
[91m│ your code. libFuzzer tries to generate this sequence of byte arrays in a way │[0m
[91m│ that maximizes test coverage.                                                │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ **Warning**: By itself libFuzzer typically does not generate valid           │[0m
[91m│ JavaScript code.                                                             │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ ## Changes to V8                                                             │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ **tldr:** Do the same as https://codereview.chromium.org/2280623002 to       │[0m
[91m│ introduce                                                                    │[0m
[91m│ a new fuzzer to V8.                                                          │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ This is a step by step guide on how to make a new fuzzer in V8. In the       │[0m
[91m│ example                                                                      │[0m
[91m│ the fuzzer is called `foo`.                                                  │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 1. Copy one of the existing fuzzer implementations in                        │[0m
[91m│ [test/fuzzer/](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/v8/test/fuzzer/), e.g.   │[0m
[91m│ `cp wasm.cc foo.cc`                                                          │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ * Copying an existing fuzzer is a good idea to get all the required setup,   │[0m
[91m│ e.g. setting up the isolate                                                  │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 2. Create a directory called `foo` in                                        │[0m
[91m│ [test/fuzzer/](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/v8/test/fuzzer/) which   │[0m
[91m│ contains at least one file                                                   │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ * The file is used by the trybots to check whether the fuzzer actually       │[0m
[91m│ compiles and runs                                                            │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 3. Copy the build rules of an existing fuzzer in                             │[0m
[91m│ [BUILD.gn](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/v8/BUILD.gn), e.g. the build │[0m
[91m│ rules for the                                                                │[0m
[91m│ [wasm.cc](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/v8/test/fuzzer/wasm.cc)       │[0m
[91m│ fuzzer                                                                       │[0m
[91m│ are `v8_source_set("wasm_fuzzer")` and `v8_fuzzer("wasm_fuzzer")`. Note that │[0m
[91m│ the name has to be the name of the directory created in Step 2 + `_fuzzer`   │[0m
[91m│ so                                                                           │[0m
[91m│ that the scripts on the trybots work                                         │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 4. Now you can already compile the fuzzer, e.g. with `ninja -j 1000 -C       │[0m
[91m│ out/x64.debug/v8_simple_foo_fuzzer`                                          │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ * Use this binary to reproduce issues found by cluster fuzz, e.g.            │[0m
[91m│ `out/x64.debug/v8_simple_foo_fuzzer testcase.foo`                            │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 5. Copy the binary name and the test directory name in                       │[0m
[91m│ [test/fuzzer/fuzzer.isolate](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/v8/test/fu │[0m
[91m│ zzer/fuzzer.isolate)                                                         │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 6. Add the fuzzer to the FuzzerTestSuite in                                  │[0m
[91m│ [test/fuzzer/testcfg.py](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/v8/test/fuzzer │[0m
[91m│ /testcfg.py)                                                                 │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ * This step is needed to run the fuzzer with the files created in Step 2 on  │[0m
[91m│ the trybots                                                                  │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 8. Commit the changes described above to the V8 repository                   │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ ## Changes to Chromium                                                       │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ **tldr:** Do the same as https://codereview.chromium.org/2344823002 to add   │[0m
[91m│ the                                                                          │[0m
[91m│ new fuzzer to cluster fuzz.                                                  │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 1. Copy the build rules of an existing fuzzer in                             │[0m
[91m│ [testing/libfuzzer/fuzzers/BUILD.gn](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/te │[0m
[91m│ sting/libfuzzer/fuzzers/BUILD.gn),                                           │[0m
[91m│ e.g. the build rule for the                                                  │[0m
[91m│ [wasm.cc](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/v8/test/fuzzer/wasm.cc)       │[0m
[91m│ fuzzer                                                                       │[0m
[91m│ is `v8_wasm_fuzzer`. There is no need to set a `dictionary` , or a           │[0m
[91m│ `seed_corpus`.                                                               │[0m
[91m│ See                                                                          │[0m
[91m│ [chromium-fuzzing-getting-started](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiu │[0m
[91m│ m/src/+/master/testing/libfuzzer/getting_started.md)                         │[0m
[91m│ for more information.                                                        │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 2. Compile the fuzzer in chromium (for different configurations see:         │[0m
[91m│ https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/master/testing/libfuzzer/re │[0m
[91m│ ference.md):                                                                 │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ * `gn gen out/libfuzzer '--args=use_libfuzzer=true is_asan=true              │[0m
[91m│ is_debug=false'`                                                             │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ * `ninja -j 1000 -C out/libfuzzer/ v8_foo_fuzzer`                            │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ 3. Run the fuzzer locally                                                    │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│ * `mkdir /tmp/empty_corpus && out/libfuzzer/v8_foo_fuzzer /tmp/empty_corpus` │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m│                                                                              │[0m
[91m└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘[0m
